    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d465">

                <pb facs="0754" n="622" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg622"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/7596: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-09-01T12:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 1,
                                1926—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received September 1—5:51
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>362. My 357, August 27, 3 p.m.</p>
                <p>1. Following from American consul general, Hankoitem: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“August 31, 10 a.m. Wu Pei-fu has suffered serious setback at the hands
                            of the Southerners and has fallen back early this morning. Southern
                            troops now very near Wuchang. Admiral Hough<anchor n="20"
                                xml:id="d465-f1"/> returning today via commercial transport. <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Isabel</hi> in Shanghai for overhauling; <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Polos</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Portage</hi> [<hi rendition="#italic">Pigeon?</hi>] now here.
                            Suggest that destroyers be sent here at once as a precautionary measure
                            since there is some danger of looting from the retreating forces. Local
                            American community requests this measure of security.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>2. I concur in suggestion regarding despatch of destroyers to Hankow and have so
                    informed commander in chief, United States Asiatic Fleet, repeating to him
                    Lockhart’s telegram aforementioned.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d465-f1" n="20" xml:id="d465-f1-content">
                <p>Rear Admiral Henry H. Hough, U. S. N., commander of the Yangtze Patrol.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
